{#
# TICK-045 vendor override: this is OpenEMR 8.3.0's real, unmodified
# templates/oauth2/oauth2-login.html.twig (confirmed against the running pinned
# container, same verification approach as the existing
# openemr_overrides/templates/oauth2/scope-authorize.html.twig override from
# TICK-037), with one addition -- the `scripts` block below.
#
# This is the login (and MFA) form a patient sees when the AI Chat portal
# panel's iframe (openemr_modules/aeai-portal-chat, always 640px-tall) needs
# re-authentication after the ai-server session expires. Full login rendered
# inside that panel is effectively unusable (neither mouse-wheel scroll nor
# keyboard Tab reliably reached past the first couple of fields --
# evidence/TICK-045/CHAT_PANEL_INVESTIGATION.md, Finding 1), and a patient who
# lands here with no visible cue that they're stuck in a tiny embedded form
# reasonably concludes "chat is broken" rather than "I need to sign in again".
#
# The `scripts` block breaks the page out to a full top-level tab whenever it
# renders inside any iframe, so re-auth is always a normal full-page sign-in
# flow instead of a form trapped in a small panel -- one of this ticket's own
# sanctioned fixes ("redirecting session-expired re-auth to a full top-level
# page instead of embedding it in the 640px panel"). No-op when this page is
# already top-level (the common case: a direct link, or after breaking out
# once already). Bind-mounted over the vendor path in docker-compose.yml, same
# pattern as the scope-authorize.html.twig override -- not a custom feature,
# just a targeted addition on top of the unmodified vendor form.
#}
{#
 # Authorization Server Member
 #
 # @package   OpenEMR
 # @link      https://www.open-emr.org
 # @author    Jerry Padgett <sjpadgett@gmail.com>
 # @author    Stephen Nielson <snielson@discoverandchange.com>
 # @copyright Copyright (c) 2020 Jerry Padgett <sjpadgett@gmail.com>
 # @copyright Copyright (c) 2023 Discover and Change, Inc. <snielson@discoverandchange.com>
 # @license   https://github.com/openemr/openemr/blob/master/LICENSE GNU General Public License 3
#}
{% extends "oauth2/oauth2-base.html.twig" %}
{% block title %}{{ "OpenEMR Authorization"|xlt }}{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}
    {#
    # TICK-047: this entire `scripts` block is duplicated, byte for byte, in both
    # openemr_overrides/templates/oauth2/oauth2-login.html.twig and
    # openemr_overrides/templates/oauth2/scope-authorize.html.twig. If you change
    # one, change the other identically -- ai_server/tests/test_oauth2_breakout_override.py
    # fails CI if the two copies ever drift apart.
    #
    # It is deliberately NOT hoisted into the shared `scripts` block of
    # oauth2-base.html.twig, which both files extend. Overriding the base would
    # mean bind-mounting a pinned copy of the vendor template that renders the
    # <head>/setupHeader/<body> skeleton for *every* OAuth2 page, so a copy left
    # stale by an OpenEMR upgrade would silently degrade all of them instead of
    # just the two pages TICK-045 verified. It would also silently extend
    # breakout to patient-select.html.twig -- the only other template extending
    # the base, which defines no `scripts` block of its own and is not reachable
    # in this deployment's portal flow, so that behavior change could not be
    # live-verified.
    #}
    <script>
        // TICK-045: break out of any embedding iframe (the AI Chat portal panel,
        // in particular) before this sign-in/consent form paints, so
        // re-authentication is always a full top-level page. See the file header
        // comment above.
        if (window.top !== window.self) {
            // TICK-046: a blocked top-level navigation is silent -- no error, no
            // event. Chrome only allows a frame to navigate the top frame without
            // a user gesture when the two are same-origin, so if this deployment's
            // topology ever puts the embedding page on a different origin than
            // this one (as it briefly did during TICK-045's live verification),
            // the assignment below simply does nothing and the patient is left
            // staring at the unusable 640px embedded form. Assume that happened if
            // this document is still here shortly afterwards, and offer a link
            // instead: a real click carries the user gesture browsers do accept
            // for a cross-origin top-level navigation.
            var aeaiBreakoutTimer = window.setTimeout(function () {
                if (document.getElementById('aeai-breakout-fallback')) {
                    return;
                }
                var link = document.createElement('a');
                link.id = 'aeai-breakout-fallback';
                link.href = window.location.href;
                link.target = '_top';
                link.textContent = 'Click here to sign in';
                link.setAttribute('style', 'position:fixed;top:0;left:0;right:0;z-index:2147483647;'
                    + 'display:block;padding:1rem;background:#842029;color:#fff;text-align:center;'
                    + 'font:bold 1rem/1.4 sans-serif;text-decoration:underline;');
                (document.body || document.documentElement).appendChild(link);
            }, 1500);
            // The top frame navigating away unloads this one, which cancels the
            // fallback. `pagehide` only fires once the new top-level document
            // commits, though, so a breakout that succeeds more slowly than the
            // timeout above will show the banner briefly on its way out. That is
            // cosmetic -- the link points at this same page -- but it is not the
            // zero-flash guarantee it may look like: the margin is the timeout
            // minus the top-level navigation's commit time (~25-80ms locally).
            window.addEventListener('pagehide', function () {
                window.clearTimeout(aeaiBreakoutTimer);
            });
            window.top.location.href = window.location.href;
        }
    </script>
{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<div class="row h-100 w-100 justify-content-center align-items-center">
    <div class="col-sm-6 bg-light text-dark">
        <div class="text-md-center">
            <h4 class="mb-4 mt-1">{% if mfaRequired %}{{'MFA Verification'|xlt }}{% else %}{{ "Sign In"|xlt  }}{% endif %}</h4>
        </div>
        <hr />
        <form method="post" name="userLogin" id="userLogin" action="{{ redirect|attr }}">
        {% if invalid is not empty %}
            <div class="alert alert-danger">
                <p>{{ invalid|text }}</p>
            </div>
        {% endif %}
            <input type="hidden" name="csrf_token_form" value="{{ csrfToken|attr }}" />
            {% if not mfaRequired %}

            {% if enforce_signin_email %}
            <div class="form-group">
                <input class="form-control" placeholder="{{ "Email if required"|xla  }}" type="email" name="email">
            </div>
            {% endif %}
            <div class="form-group">
                <input class="form-control" placeholder="{{ "Registered username"|xla  }}" type="text" name="username" value="">
            </div>
            <div class="form-group">
                <input class="form-control" placeholder="******" type="password" name="password" value="">
            </div>
            {% endif %}

            {% if mfaRequired %}
                {% if isTOTP %}
                <fieldset>
                    <legend>{{'Provide TOTP code'|xlt }}</legend>
                </fieldset>
                <div class="form-group">
                    <input class="form-control" id="totp_token" autocomplete="false" placeholder="{{ "Enter required authentication code"|xla  }}" type="text" name="mfa_token">
                </div>
                <div class="form-group">
                    <button type="submit" name="user_role" class="btn btn-primary btn-save" value="api">{{ "Authenticate TOTP"|xlt }}</button>
                </div>
                {% endif %}

                {% if isU2F %}
                <div class="form-group">
                    <fieldset>
                        <legend>{{ 'Insert U2F Key'|xlt  }}</legend>
                        <div>
                            <ul>
                                <li>{{ 'Insert your key into a USB port and click the Authenticate button below.'|xlt  }}</li>
                                <li>{{ 'Then press the flashing button on your key within 1 minute.'|xlt }}</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </fieldset>
                    <button type="button" id="authutf" class="btn btn-primary btn-save" onclick="doAuth()">{{ 'Authenticate U2F'|xlt  }}</button>
                    <input type="hidden" name="form_requests" value="{{ u2fRequests|attr }}" />
                    <input type="hidden" name="user_role" value="api">
                </div>
                {% endif %}

                {% if enforce_signin_email %}
                <div class="form-group">
                    <input class="form-control" type="hidden" value="{{ user.email|attr }}">
                </div>
                {% endif %}
                <div class="form-group">
                    <input class="form-control" type="hidden" name="username" value="{{ user.username|attr }}">
                </div>
                <div class="form-group">
                    <input class="form-control" type="hidden" name="password" value="{{ user.password|attr }}">
                </div>
                <input class="form-control" type="hidden" name="mfa_type" value="TOTP">
            {% endif %}
            <hr />
            <div class="row">
                <div class="col-md-12">
                    <div class="btn-group">
                        {% if mfaRequired is empty %}
                            <button type="submit" name="user_role" class="btn btn-outline-primary" value="api">{{"OpenEMR Login"|xlt }} <i class="fa fa-sign-in-alt"></i></button>
                            {% if patientRoleSupport is not empty %}
                                <button type="submit" name="user_role" class="btn btn-outline-info" value="portal-api">{{ "Patient Login"|xlt  }} <i class="fa fa-sign-in-alt"></i></button>
                            {% endif %}
                        {% endif %}
                    </div>
                    <div class="form-check-inline float-right">
                        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="persist_login" id="persist_login" value="1">
                        <label for="persist_login" class="form-check-label">{{ "Remember Me"|xlt  }}</label>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </form>
    </div>
</div>
<script>
    function doAuth() {
        let xl = window.top.xl || function(id) { return id; };
        let f = document.getElementById("userLogin");
        let requests = [];
        try {
            requests = JSON.parse(f.form_requests.value);
            if (!(Array.isArray(requests) && requests.length > 0 && requests[0].challenge)) {
                throw "Invalid U2F request data";
            }
        }
        catch (error) {
            console.error("Internal error: invalid U2f request data.  This should never happen", error);
            alert(xl("Internal error: invalid U2F request data"));
            return;
        }
        // The server's getAuthenticateData() repeats the same challenge in all requests.
        let challenge = requests[0].challenge;
        const registeredKeys = (requests || []).map(req => ({"version": req.version, "keyHandle": req.keyHandle}));
        u2f.sign({{ appId|json_encode }}, challenge, registeredKeys,
            function (data) {
                if (data.errorCode && data.errorCode != 0) {
                    alert(xl("Key access failed with error") +' ' + data.errorCode);
                    return;
                }
                //hide totp input if both on used
                const totpTokenElement = document.getElementById('totp_token');
                if (totpTokenElement) {
                    totpTokenElement.style.display = 'none';
                }
                //create new mfa_token input
                let elInput = document.createElement('input');
                elInput.setAttribute('type', 'hidden');
                elInput.setAttribute('name', 'mfa_token');
                elInput.setAttribute('value', JSON.stringify(data));
                f.appendChild(elInput);
                f.mfa_type.value = 'U2F';
                f.submit();
            },
            60
    );
    }

</script>
{% endblock %}
